WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.260
The best sports breads from the Monaco Cup semifinals,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.780
<i>Japan</i> and <i>Gopan</i>,
were offered to the F1 racers.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:15.030
The victorious F1 driver judged Shadow’s paella <i>Gopan</i> to be better than Kazuma’s.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.950
Kazuma then tried to approach Shadow, but...

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.540
Shadow made fun of him with his strange behavior.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.080
Say, Shadow.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.170
Its proclamation leaving various uncertainties,

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.550
the topic for the finals was announced.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:36.850
That topic was divided into three matches, based on the themes of clothing, food and shelter.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.770
Then...

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.270
The theme of the first match,
a well-molded bread, goes to Suwabara.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.270
The theme of the second match,
dinner bread, goes to Kawachi.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.820
The theme of the third match, a bread with
the taste of your homeland, goes to Azuma.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:53.950
Let’s aim to win!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.450
All right!

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.410
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.290
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.580
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:08.050
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:13.220
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.640
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.100
Naked, naked, naked!!

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.980
The magnificent bread match!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.540
It looks like he’s really getting into the spirit for the finals.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.420
Spirit, huh?

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.330
Well, it sure does look that way, but...

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.670
Why’s he practicing his swordsmanship in the middle of a busy public road?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.920
I mean, does that have anything to do with bread?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.890
Well, I don’t know.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.140
But, I’m sure that he put
some thought into that practice.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.520
Do you think so?

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.270
More importantly, how about worrying about yourself?

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:36.400
Azuma has locked himself in his room, and
seems to be thinking about it in his own way.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.280
You’re the only one not doing anything.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:42.040
Stop thinking of ways to
conceal your baldness with wimpy wigs,

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.490
and think about bread a little!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.990
What are you doing?!

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.790
Give it back!

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.410
Ryou!
Give it back!

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.750
Please give it back!
Ryou!

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.670
The ordering of the combatants for
the American team has been announced.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:53.840
Is that so?

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.340
It seems that the first match will be Monica Adenauer,

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.890
the second match will be Spencer Henley Hokou,

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.130
and the third match will be Shadow White.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.060
Azuma will be facing Shadow, huh?

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.070
My opponent is <i>that</i> Shachihoko, huh?

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:15.990
Look up!

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:19.290
Secret technique,
Dragon Twister Technique!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:28.370
The second match is Shachihoko,
and the third match is Shadow.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:33.370
That means, Monica must be that
silent girl, since she’s the only one left.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.470
I hoped that I could cross swords
with the Shadow who beat Azuma,

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.880
but of all people, to think that I’m stuck with the girl...

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.380
Well, it can’t be helped.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.850
No matter who the opponent might be, all I have to do is put all of my soul into winning.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.850
With my <i>Lupan</i> #1, Pane di oro Kai.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.670
Say, Spencer...

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.120
What kind of sound is that?!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.170
No, it’s just that...

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:14.340
This is the first time you’ve spoken.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.830
So, what brought this about?

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.210
That’s because Shadow isn’t here.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:23.340
It’s annoying to have him imitate me,
so I just haven’t spoken until now.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.340
It’s not like I’m the silent type.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:30.440
More importantly, my opponent, Kai Suwabara...

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.350
Is that Samurai Boy strong?

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.690
Yeah, he’s really strong.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:38.810
He was the favorite of the Pantasia newcomers’ battle.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.580
Oh?

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:47.870
Well, I don’t think that there’s even the
slightest chance of your losing at this theme.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.370
Just don’t let your guard down, though.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.830
Wh-What’re you doing?

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:57.540
Don’t ever touch my snacks.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.420
Aside from my life, I love candy the most.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:14.930
Why’s there so little information
available on the American representatives?

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.570
No matter how much I search, the only information I get is on Shachihoko.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:25.450
I can’t find a single thing on Monica or Shadow.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.700
Yeah, I noticed that as well.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.660
Huh?

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:33.160
If may be that this is the first time the two of them are appearing in a bread tournament.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.620
That can’t be!

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.670
It isn’t possible for amateurs like that to come
all the way to the finals in a world tournament.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.760
However, it’s not like the possibility is zero...

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.670
What do you mean?

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.380
Well...

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.480
Phone call, Monsieur.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:49.760
For me?

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.640
Hello.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.770
Hey, Ryou.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.060
Do you know who this is?

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.230
Th-That voice is...!

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:56.810
Kid?!

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.860
Is it Kid?!

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:00.320
That’s right!

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.360
That’s my genius!

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.810
It’s been a while, Ryou.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:09.330
A little birdie told me that you were investigating
a woman called Monica and a guy called Shadow.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.820
So, I thought I’d help out and called you.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.660
Help out?!

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.330
What are you doing these days?!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:19.830
These days, I’m running a little
investigative company in New York.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.300
I still haven’t found out anything about the Shadow guy,

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.970
but it was easy to find out
about that woman.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.090
Really?

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.340
That would be really helpful.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.900
So, who is she?

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:34.350
That woman named Monica Adenauer is...

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.410
That’s all I know.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.650
Hey, Ryou!

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.700
This is Kid.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.080
Are you all right?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.330
Allo? It’s “allo” in French, right?

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.530
Coming, Kid’s coming... he’s definitely coming.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.280
What’s wrong, Ryou?!

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:58.790
Sophie...

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.390
Call everybody here right now.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.210
What do you want?

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:09.210
We’re all practicing hard for the finals right now.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.960
So, keep it short.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.710
Yeah, Kuro-yan.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:16.880
After being told off by you, I locked myself up in my room, and was thinking of bread.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.510
Did you think of anything?

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.980
Don’t stray from the point.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.480
Sorry... but this is important.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:30.650
First, why do you suppose that the owner of St. Pierre

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.030
hasn’t sabotaged us in any way after the semifinals?

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:37.490
Well, that’s probably because it was
hard to do so without getting caught, right?

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:39.610
That’s not it.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.700
It’s because he no longer needs to.

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.740
What do you mean?

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.750
Initially, the American team
consisted of only Shachihoko.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:49.660
But, you’ve noticed what
happened after the semifinals, right?

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.970
Shachihoko was reassigned
to third position amongst them.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:57.920
I believe that’s because
there were two talented amateurs

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:01.480
who quickly learned from
experience during the tournament.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.010
Huh?!

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:04.480
That’s even harder to understand.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.480
The owner of St. Pierre...

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.800
discovered two amateurs with tremendous innate talent for breadmaking,

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.600
and recruited them.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:15.860
By teaming them up with the
talented and experienced Shachihoko,

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.070
he had the two of them mature during the tournament.

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:21.450
Wh... Why do something troublesome like that?

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:25.420
It’s most difficult to find talented young bakers.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:29.660
He probably decided that even
though they’re complete amateurs,

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.460
it’d be best to raise talented people like that himself.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.080
Ridiculous!

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:36.590
You called us out here to tell us something like this?!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.720
I’m going back.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.220
Ridiculous?

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.350
But... will you be able to say the same thing after hearing this fact?

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:49.140
Your opponent, Monica Adenauer.

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:54.230
She holds the title of “Champion of the
59th World Pastry Chef Competition.”

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.660
In other words, she’s the world’s Queen of Patisserie.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.490
Huh?!

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:11.080
Your opponent, Monica Adenauer.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.760
She holds the title of “Champion of the
59th World Pastry Chef Competition.”

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:18.010
In other words, she’s the world’s Queen of Patisserie.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.010
Huh?!

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.260
What?!

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:24.270
So... so, what difference does that make?

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.970
Though she may be the queen in the world of pastry,

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:30.010
when it comes to the world of bread, I’m superior!

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.770
I couldn’t possibly lose
to such an amateur!

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.280
It’s to “such an amateur” that Shachihoko lost.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.860
Compared to bread artisans,

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.500
those in the world of the patissier lay great stress on the training

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:43.790
required to make their creations beautiful.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:48.450
With regard to the theme of the first
match, making a beautifully molded bread,

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:52.790
I wouldn’t be exaggerating if I said that her
skill is that of the top bakers of the world.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.300
Suwabara’s trembling.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:56.930
It’s not surprising.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:11:00.640
He ended up with someone like the
Queen of Patisserie as his opponent.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.300
I’d want to run away in these circumstances.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.060
Are you all right, Suwabara?

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.490
It’s trembling.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:13.070
My soul’s trembling!

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:18.570
It’s the first time that I’ve trembled with excitement like this.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:20.790
You wanted to know if I’m all right, Azuma?

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:25.530
I’m so happy right now,
I could die from this trembling.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:31.590
I’m participating in this tournament to battle strong artisans from all around the world,

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:37.050
so when I learned that the little girl is to be my
last opponent, truth be told, I was disappointed.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.050
But, to think that she was the
queen of the patisserie world...

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.850
I have no complaints
regarding my opponent.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.440
That makes it a true final for a world tournament.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:49.030
I must thank the owner of St. Pierre.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:54.900
Takes all kinds to make a world...

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.250
Yeah.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:01.450
While there are people like Azuma, who
head straight towards fulfilling their dream...

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.150
Others, like him, concern themselves over only their wins and losses,

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.870
in order to better themselves.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:10.050
And... then there are unfathomable baldies, like you.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:10.970
Yeah...

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.130
What, you got some kind of problem with that?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.630
If you have a problem, then win once in a while.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.470
Even if Suwabara’s all fired up about it,

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:24.650
it’s questionable as to whether he can win
against the Queen of Patisserie at that theme.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:30.610
Should both you and Suwabara lose, without Azuma even having a chance to appear,

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:32.640
Japan will be finished.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.860
Don’t forget that the spot that
you hold in the second match...

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:39.360
is the key position in the winning of this tournament.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.510
The finals are in a week.

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:57.050
If I put my soul into this,
it will be complete.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:13:03.260
The champion’s crown that I’ll steal from
the little girl and place on my own head.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.770
One week later

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:16.530
Just as you’d expect of the
finals, they’ve really gone all out.

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:17.600
It’s a band!

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:22.610
But, even though it’s the finals,
there isn’t much of an audience.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:28.870
When it’s like this, I sort of understand Rame’s
feelings in wanting the home team France to win.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.450
Ridiculous!

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:34.670
The true spectators are not the
crowds that come to cheer a team,

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:37.380
but those who come to
observe the quality of the match.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.510
Just having low-level spectators around is annoying.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:44.970
With only true spectators here, we
now have a crowd suitable for the finals.

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:46.430
Yo!

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.050
If you don’t intend on
watching seriously, then go back home!

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.720
If not, I’ll cut you apart.

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:52.610
Geez.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:53.940
Impudent fools.

00:13:58.030 --> 00:13:59.650
Samurai Boy...

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.410
N... Naked woman!

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:05.990
What do you mean, “naked woman”?

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.870
My name is Monica.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.410
Monica Adenauer.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.460
What the hell are you trying to pull?!

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:13.040
This isn’t the beach!

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.620
I can dress however I choose, right?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.960
Even you, a finalist, are planning on sullying the sacred finals?!

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:26.470
So, are you going to cut me up as well?

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:28.060
Like, this part here?

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.220
Or this part here?

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:35.860
Just as I thought, this
samurai boy’s a straight-laced guy

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:37.690
who’s had little experience with women.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:41.940
My plan is to confuse him with my
sexiness so that he loses the match.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:45.870
Well, I don’t really think I’d lose,
even if I didn’t do something like this,

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:47.450
but it doesn’t hurt to be careful.

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:52.700
In order to ensure that my dream of
building a candy castle is fulfilled 100%.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.840
You want me to participate in a bread tournament?

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:57.210
Hey, old man...

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:59.340
I’m a pastry chef.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.920
Yeah, I know.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:06.550
But, St. Pierre has plans to open up a patisserie branch.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:11.900
If you win in that tournament, the Monaco Cup,

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:17.770
I think it’d be a good idea to give you
the post of General Manager of that branch.

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.570
That’s right.

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:23.810
That would truly be the place that
would become your candy castle.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.000
Candy castle!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.520
While I may be the world champion,

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:34.070
being able to have a store of my own at my age isn’t easy.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:38.540
This is a great opportunity, for
getting my hands on my castle!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.790
In order to do that, this man must...

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.500
Right, Samurai Boy?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.420
In that case...!

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.220
With this, we’re even!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.730
What do you mean, “we’re even”?!

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:58.720
What’s with this guy, he’s really weird!

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.400
He really hates to lose, no
matter how strange things get.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.730
It really takes all kinds to make a world.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:08.320
Ladies and gentlemen.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.240
Welcome to the first match of the finals.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.420
Uh, although there are not many of you out there...

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:19.380
The second match is in one week,
and the third match is in two weeks.

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:25.420
Let us have fun fun fun for these two finals weeks!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:29.420
Here we have the Japanese representative:
Naked Samurai, Kai Suwabara,

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.430
and the American representative:
Naked Girl, Monica Adenauer.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:36.810
The time limit is 5 hours.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:40.520
In that naked state, you can
take your time baking amour!

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.020
It’s finally time.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:45.230
Yeah.

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:46.980
Suwabara.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.500
If you lose,

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:54.740
we’ll have to depend on the win of this baldy,

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.450
who hasn’t even noticed that his wig has slipped so much.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.450
A loss is unforgivable.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:00.750
Oh!

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.210
Suwabara has two sets of dough,

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.710
and for some reason, their
consistencies and volumes are different!

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:12.710
The big bowl is syrupy, and
seems to contain a lot of egg yolk.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:16.720
The dough in the smaller
bowl is clearly croissant dough.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.100
Wait and see, you damned naked woman.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:27.110
By combining these two sets of dough,
I’ll create the most supreme radiance.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:31.110
You’ll learn of the magnificence
of my <i>Lupan</i> #1, Pane di oro Kai!

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:32.620
Oh?

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:35.610
Just take a look at what’s on Adenauer’s countertop.

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:39.210
She has prepared five different sets of dough!

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:40.080
What?!

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:43.580
Here, it looks like the volumes of all five
sets of dough are approximately the same.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.080
Hey, Kuro-yan.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:49.090
Overall, I don’t quite get what Suwabara is doing, but...

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:51.680
I understand what Monica’s doing even less.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:55.590
I mean, is there any meaning to
splitting the same dough into five bowls?

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:58.020
Are your eyes merely empty holes?!

00:17:58.020 --> 00:17:59.550
That’s why you’re a slipped wig.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.600
Those five sets of dough aren’t the same.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:04.520
Look carefully.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:08.450
By looking at the color of the dough,
it’s clear that rye has been mixed in.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.610
But, they’re all of different shades.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.320
That’s true!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:16.040
That’s proof that the amount of
rye in all five of them is different.

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:20.250
Rye bread originated in Germany,
so a German may know of some trick.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:20.870
Huh?

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:24.800
I know that rye bread originated in Germany, but...

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.710
Who’s the German that you’re talking about?

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.330
Monica is the American representative.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:31.840
Yeah... A slipped wig like you wouldn’t know.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.840
Adenauer is a surname of German origin.

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:38.810
Actually, most of the immigrants in America are German,

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:41.310
and constitute about 23% of the American population.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.310
Politicians like Bush and Rumsfeld,

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:47.570
and former presidents like Roosevelt
and Eisenhower, are of German origin.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.560
Just as you’d expect of Kuro-yan.
You’re just like a triviabot.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.370
And you’re just a slipped wig.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:57.360
I got a little smarter today.

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:00.830
The only way that a pastry chef like me, still new to this field,

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:05.370
can compete with world class bakers is with this rye bread.

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:12.800
This rye bread, which my mother
would often make when I was young.

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.890
Here you go, Monica.

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:16.560
The rye bread’s done.

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:17.300
I don’t want it!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:20.800
Oh Monica, you’re chewing on gum again?

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:23.100
Because we’re just having bread again, right?

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:26.310
In that case, I prefer to have sweet things.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:27.860
That’s not good.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:30.310
If you don’t eat proper food, it’ll be bad for your body.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:32.280
Proper food?

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:35.820
Simply eating bread without anything on
the side is just as bad for your body, isn’t it?

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:37.570
Monica!

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.030
I’m sorry, Monica.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.370
But, we’re now going to go to live in America, the land of freedom and opportunity.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.580
I’m sure that your father’s dream, to
make a candy castle, will come true.

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:50.670
Then, we can bid goodbye to living in poverty like this.

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:51.540
Really?!

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.580
Yes, really, Monica.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.260
Papa!

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:58.090
The candy castle is also your dream, right?

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:02.650
I’ll be sure to fulfill that dream
in America for your sake as well.

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:05.230
So, don’t complain for now.

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:06.800
Please eat your mother’s bread.

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:08.060
Okay!

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.150
What’s this? It’s delicious!

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:15.310
It isn’t like the usual bread!

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:18.330
Well, you’d get tired of eating
the same bread all the time, right?

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:20.070
So, I applied a trick to it.

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:22.950
Be patient for a little while longer, Monica.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:27.580
Once we’re in America, I’ll
make lots of yummy stuff for you.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:33.080
But, our life in America wasn’t easy.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.080
Nobody accepted Papa’s pastries.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.890
He collapsed from being overworked,

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:40.090
and Mama was hospitalized from worrying too much.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.180
Papa, Mama...

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.640
I don’t like this.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.090
I won’t lose.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:48.600
Papa and my dream castle... Our candy castle...

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:51.660
I’ll be sure to build it...

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:54.330
On this continent of America.

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:59.030
That dream is now close to becoming a reality.

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.530
Samurai Boy...

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.780
I don’t know what you’re up to,

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.490
but I won’t let you get in the way of my dream.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.370
Oh? Oh? Oh, oh?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.490
What is that?!

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.990
Suwabara’s fruit are shining brightly.

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:15.500
What is... that radiance?!

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:17.500
That’s pretty.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:19.340
Kuro-yan?

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:22.970
It looks like the surface has
been covered with syrup, but...

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:25.300
With just that, you wouldn’t get that much of a shine.

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:26.690
This is...

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:29.820
We might be able to see a new, never-before-seen variety of Suwabara’s bread.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:37.520
How in the world did such radiance...

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:42.860
This isn’t the time to be impressed, Monica.

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:44.450
Samurai Boy...

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:48.200
I may have underestimated you a little, like candy.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:51.130
In that case, I’ll show you what I can do.

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:53.580
The reason that I’m the world champion.

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:59.090
These jewels are the secret behind <i>Lupan</i> #1.

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:00.970
Th-Th-Th-This is...!

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:03.590
T-T-Truly art!

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:05.840
You exaggerate.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:08.180
This candy sculpture!

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:10.360
Candy sculpture?

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:13.320
Wh-What is that?!

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:21.690
This candy sculpture looks like it is alive!

00:24:07.310 --> 00:24:09.260
Because of its extreme deliciousness, Pierrot’s crying.

00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:12.310
Because of its extreme
deliciousness, Pierrot’s been arrested!

00:24:12.310 --> 00:24:13.700
But, why?!

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:15.030
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.030 --> 00:24:16.030
Pierrot escorted away!?

00:24:16.030 --> 00:24:17.700
The bread packed tightly with love!

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:18.830
Be sure to watch!

00:24:18.830 --> 00:24:19.920
Yeah.

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:22.650
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.140 --> 00:24:26.310
In French, chefs who specialize in making pastries are called “patissier.”

00:24:26.310 --> 00:24:29.370
Originally, it referred to those who made pâté cuisine

00:24:29.370 --> 00:24:31.640
using pie dough containing minced fish or meat.

00:24:32.170 --> 00:24:34.300
Oh?!
